      "summary": "An untouched tombstone still settles late-committed after 2 x TTL (slow call 2.65 s, TTL 1 s); README says late settlement applies only 'within one more timeout' and not-active after. Tombstones drop lazily on the next call that touches the scope. Over-counts (safe direction); docs/behaviour mismatch.",
      "resolution": "docs fix: README settlement table, reclaim paragraph and unit-test summary, plus CHANGELOG #17 entry, now state the tombstone is held for at least one more timeout and dropped on the next touch after that; policy code unchanged"
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "case": "8",
      "summary": "Observed 12/200 admitted at envoy concurrency 4 (= 4 x 3) and 3/200 at concurrency 1, matching README's N x aggregateBudget. FLEX_SERVICE_ENVOY_CONCURRENCY=1 gives one budget per replica; README could say so.",
      "resolution": "docs fix: README single-worker note (PR #40)"
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "case": "2",
      "summary": "Client ID Enforcement could not be exercised in local mode (needs control-plane contracts); http-basic-authentication-flex used as the upstream authentication policy. Ordering and spoof-resistance proven; Client-ID-specific run still pending on a connected gateway.",
      "resolution": "open"
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "case": "8b",
      "found_utc": "2026-10-02",
      "summary": "The gateway applies its config twice at startup, about 5 s apart. The second apply replaces the listener; Envoy builds new wasm VMs, so every ledger resets. Mac: a scope exhausted before the apply (12 admitted on 4 ledgers) was admitted again after it at total=800/1600/2400, then denied at 3200. Linux CI runner: the first burst straddled the apply (applies 1 -> 2 during the burst) and reached 8 ledgers, admitting 20 of 200. README said a restart was the only reset. Over-admit direction. Startup is the only trigger confirmed. Follow-up 2026-10-03 (case 2d): a UI Save & Apply with no config change on a connected gateway applied config (4 -> 5) but did NOT reset the ledger (exhausted client still denied, would-be-total=3200). A policy config change remains untested.",
      "resolution": "docs fix: README restart paragraph and limitations, CHANGELOG #15 entry and known limitations now say a restart or a config apply that rebuilds the listener resets the ledger; case 8 waits for the second apply; case 8b records the reset; policy code unchanged"
    }
  ],
